{"_set": "items", "question_id": "mvar_cf432d_5", "model": "claude-opus-5", "problem_id": "mvar_cf432d", "family": "multivariate_regression", "type": "two_choice_loss_compare", "metric": "test_mse", "ratio": 1.816, "correct": "A", "answer": "A", "is_correct": true, "raw_response": "**Calibration from references:**\n\n- Adagrad shows a clear trend: lr 0.1 → 0.906 (too high, diverging), lr 0.03 → 0.192 (best), lr 0.01 → 0.199, lr 0.003 → 0.289 (already degrading from being too slow). Extrapolating downward, Adagrad at lr 0.001 would be badly undertrained in 640 steps — Adagrad's accumulating denominator shrinks effective step size fast, so at lr 0.001 the model barely moves from initialization. Expect loss well above 0.29, likely ~0.6–0.9.\n- RMSprop at lr 0.001 is near its standard sweet spot (RMSprop/Adam-family optima typically ~1e-3). AdamW at lr 0.1 gave 0.868 (way too high), which tells us adaptive methods here blow up at large lr but should be fine at 1e-3. Expect RMSprop lr 0.001 to land around 0.1–0.2, competitive with or better than the best Adagrad reference.\n\nSo the RMSprop setting should clearly beat the near-frozen Adagrad setting.\n\n**A**", "content": "**Calibration from references:**\n\n- Adagrad shows a clear trend: lr 0.1 → 0.906 (too high, diverging), lr 0.03 → 0.192 (best), lr 0.01 → 0.199, lr 0.003 → 0.289 (already degrading from being too slow). Extrapolating downward, Adagrad at lr 0.001 would be badly undertrained in 640 steps — Adagrad's accumulating denominator shrinks effective step size fast, so at lr 0.001 the model barely moves from initialization. Expect loss well above 0.29, likely ~0.6–0.9.\n- RMSprop at lr 0.001 is near its standard sweet spot (RMSprop/Adam-family optima typically ~1e-3). AdamW at lr 0.1 gave 0.868 (way too high), which tells us adaptive methods here blow up at large lr but should be fine at 1e-3. Expect RMSprop lr 0.001 to land around 0.1–0.2, competitive with or better than the best Adagrad reference.\n\nSo the RMSprop setting should clearly beat the near-frozen Adagrad setting.\n\n**A**", "reasoning_content": ""}
